  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobilizing human capacity towards effective management of biodiversity and geodiversity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Maghreb region holds 18 UNESCO biosphere reserves, and 1 UNESCO Global Geopark distributed in 5 countries. These landmarks bring together clusters of a variety of ecosystems typical to the Mediterranean and Saharan habitats. UNESCO biosphere Reserves foster a holistic approach to conservation, and promote solutions reconciling the conservation of biodiversity with its sustainable use while contributing to the SDGs2030, the Multilateral Environmental Agreements, and the Sendai Framework on Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030. 
Consisting of a dynamic and interactive network of sites, the Maghreb region holds relics of ecosystems which call for their protection.  The specificity of the region calls for an investigation on the socio-ecological and economic dynamics of the communities living within and beyond these sites. The multidimensional approaches entail drawing transdisciplinary pathways to top-up institutional capacities, governance empowerment and to generate knowledge products,  and establish interlinkages between the different public and private sectors, and propel a culture of living in harmony with nature and reconciling with the natural world. 
The components of the workplan aim to co-design and develop an inclusive agile model to ensure the effective management of biodiversity and geodiversity in the Maghreb Region, in order to comply with their major functions.</narrative>
  </description>
